  "body": "`StockEye::new` took about 430 ms on the UI thread before the first frame. It now runs on a worker thread. The shell takes the eye on a later frame, as the browser shell does. Until then the viewport draws the stock sheet.\n\nReadings (Windows 11, DX12, release): the window first answers at 730/806/1079 ms before and 344/369/448 ms after.\n\n## Testing\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base main` on head a4fbc0a47, with `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4`: 10 steps, 0 failed. `ui suites: lib`: 1479 passed. The 8 integration suites passed.\n\nThe crash of #3589: on this head, an earlier run of `ui suites: lib` with the same job count ended with STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION (0xc0000005) and no FAILED test. I ran the step again, as the maintainers describe on #3589. With a valid build the step ran 2 times on this head: 1 crash (#3589) and 1 green run (1479 passed, 0 failed). The crash also happens on plain `main` (see #3589).\n\nRun by name with `cargo xtask gate test <name> --crate camcraft-ui --exact`, all ok:\n- `nothing_yet_keeps_the_receiver`\n- `a_refusal_is_handed_over_once`\n- `a_thread_that_ended_without_a_result_is_named`\n- `the_eye_can_cross_threads` (`StockEye` is `Send`)\n\nWith 16 jobs the step `ui build (--no-run)` failed in some runs with \"invalid metadata files\" for a dependency crate. It did not fail with 4 jobs. I think it is a separate build-cache problem on my machine.\n\nNot exercised: clippy (not installed here), macOS, Linux, the other gate tiers, the traced-stock view on the first frames (not looked at by eye), closing the window while the eye is still building.\n\nChangelog: The window answers sooner after start.\nRefs #3583\n\nThe full lib step is affected by a test-process crash (STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION) that also happens on plain `main`; it is tracked in #3589.\n\nThe invalid-metadata build errors of the gate at 16 jobs are tracked in #3601.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
